Buffer::writeUnsynchronized for append-only uniform rings.

- include/rive/renderer/ore/ore_buffer.hpp: Ore Buffer: writeUnsynchronized(data, size, offset, discard) for an append-only uniform ring that binds one buffer at many dynamic offsets within a frame. It writes [offset, offset + size) of the storage already bound, without the orphan update() does when the buffer was bound since its last update, because the caller guarantees no recorded command reads that range. discard marks the first write of a new use of the buffer: storage the GPU may still read is replaced without copying, so every byte outside the written range becomes undefined. The bound-since-update state is left alone, so a later update() still orphans. The base default is update(), correct but slow, which is what GL (glBufferSubData at the offset, implicitly synchronized) and D3D12 use. Contract the ring relies on: within a frame each range is written at most once and only before the commands reading it are recorded, since on WebGPU every queued write lands before that frame's submit
- source/renderer/ore/metal/ore_buffer_metal.hpp: Ore Metal buffer: declare the writeUnsynchronized override (see the ore_buffer.hpp entry)
- source/renderer/ore/metal/ore_buffer_metal.mm: Ore Metal buffer writeUnsynchronized: memcpy into the current shared backing at the offset, no orphan and no carry-forward copy. With discard, a current backing whose last bound serial is above completedSerial (the GPU may still read it) is swapped for a completed or new backing through acquireFreshBacking(0, m_size), whose whole-buffer range skips the copy; on allocation failure it writes in place like update(). m_boundSinceUpdate is never touched
- source/renderer/ore/vulkan/ore_buffer_vulkan.hpp: Ore Vulkan buffer: declare the writeUnsynchronized override (see the ore_buffer.hpp entry)
- source/renderer/ore/vulkan/ore_buffer_vulkan.cpp: Ore Vulkan buffer writeUnsynchronized: memcpy into the persistently mapped current backing at the offset, no orphan and no copy. With discard, a pooled current backing that acquireFreshBacking would not consider retired (frameStamp above safeFrameNumber or not before currentFrameNumber) is swapped for a retired or new one through acquireFreshBacking(0, m_size), which skips the copy and updates the mirrored handles. Staging buffers (empty pool) never swap. m_boundSinceUpdate is never touched
- source/renderer/ore/wgpu/ore_buffer_wgpu.hpp: Ore WebGPU buffer: declare the writeUnsynchronized override (see the ore_buffer.hpp entry); discard is unused
- source/renderer/ore/wgpu/ore_buffer_wgpu.cpp: Ore WebGPU buffer writeUnsynchronized: queue a WriteBuffer of just the range into the current backing, no orphan. Queue writes are ordered after the previous frame submit and land before this frame's, and ring ranges never overlap within a frame, so discard is a no-op. offset and size must be multiples of 4, as WriteBuffer requires. The CPU shadow is kept in sync so a later orphaning update() rewrites the ring bytes instead of stale or zero ones
- source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_buffer_d3d11.hpp: Ore D3D11 buffer: declare the writeUnsynchronized override (see the ore_buffer.hpp entry)
- source/renderer/ore/d3d11/ore_buffer_d3d11.cpp: Ore D3D11 buffer writeUnsynchronized: Map with WRITE_DISCARD when discard, else WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE, and write only the range; the shadow copy is kept in sync for a later partial update(). Precondition for constant buffers: D3D11_FEATURE_DATA_D3D11_OPTIONS::MapNoOverwriteOnDynamicConstantBuffer (NO_OVERWRITE on a dynamic CB) and ConstantBufferOffsetting (VS/PSSetConstantBuffers1 for the dynamic offsets); YUP must not call it on a uniform buffer without both. The first write of a buffer's use must be a discard. A failed Map is asserted and returns without writing

